		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: After 15 years of people asking - Why is Bullet documentation still so very bad?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43144#p43144"><![CDATA[
Fair comment, I hadn't really considered the driving force being academic research and the implications therein. I'd assumed it was more a labour of love on the part of the primary author and others. I'm not saying it isn't both of course.<br><br>It's a pity that knowledge is being repeatedly gained and lost but appreciate the circumstances you describe.<br><br>Of course I shouldn't complain, as I've got a great piece of free software, irrespective of the state of the docs. <br>So perhaps I should just thank the authors and leave it at that.<br><br>Cheers.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11736">Octavius_Ace</a> — Thu Oct 15, 2020 11:50 pm</p><hr />
